welcome to the thankful Thursday I  believe as entrepreneurs is important to  thank the people in your life who's had  an impact to help believe in you because  you can't do this alone and it's nice  just to every now and then reach out and  say thank you make them feel appreciated  so today i want to thank Brian Simon and  brian is a photographer friend of mine  here in Toronto int city he's helped me  with the number of different projects  who was a photographer at my wedding  he's got a pretty new business called  tarsi pic studios and I wanted to thank  him because Brian always goes way above  and beyond to make sure that his clients  are happy so I wanted to give a quick  example and this could be a lesson for  entrepreneurs as well so at my wedding I  wanted to give out wedding favors that  that weren't boring you know most  wedding favors are super boring it's a  it's a picture of the bride and groom in  a frame and and what am I supposed to do  without it's just to put that on my  mantel my supposed to hang on my wall am  I really gonna hang your wedding picture  on my wall right it's not going to  happen and so what I wanted to do is  make it more about the guests make it  about the people who are coming out and  give them something special that had  them on it so that they could actually  cherish that moment that they sent with  us that day I fought back to a photo  shoot that I did just on my own with  Nina I saw this picture of JFK and his  wife Jackie and I just liked how they  were sitting and I looked in you know we  got to do something similar let's let's  do something like that and i shot the  picture and I remembered that for the  wedding because I thought hey people  coming out to this wedding you know  they're all dressed up during their  suits and ties you're in there then  there are nice dresses how often you get  a professional photographer to take a  good picture of you when you're all  dressed up and looking nice not that  often so what I thought was here let's  take this JFK concept and take pictures  of everybody who was coming out to the  wedding so they could have that same  experience that we had so I told Brian  Brian I have this crazy idea okay i want  to make baseball cards with this pose  JFK couple shot on the front and  on the back I want to show candid shots  of that guests at the wedding at the  reception at the hall who are ever and  now this is having a lot of stress and  pressure on Brian because usually  photographer they come out they just  shoot the bride and groom a couple extra  shots and they're following them around  here he had to take pictures of  everybody you know that the set shot JFK  shot as well as all these other  candidate shots we can make an  individualized baseball card for  everybody so this is what it looks like  this is a buddy of mine John now I  haven't seen John for a while so I still  have to give him his card but this is  the the after result so this is him and  his girlfriend and then on the back is  not just pictures of us it's pictures of  him and his girlfriend that was kind of  before they came and then at the wedding  and then us all together and so it's a  nice memorable car that they can keep or  give them a little standard it can put  it up on their mental or desk whatever  and this is something that if I got this  from somebody I would actually keep this  like this is actually pretty cool it's a  nice memory from the wedding and that  was all thanks to Brian now Brian had to  take all these pictures then he had to  make the card right what pictures gonna  go on the front what's going to go on  the back then he had the source where  we're going to get the card from and  then aren't my related was putting them  in the cases so I didn't have that hard  a job but that was Brian right Brian  goes above and beyond he's never done  that he's never made baseball cards he's  never had to take pictures of everybody  out of wedding and he's like yeah let's  do it I'm on board he's excited because  he wants to WoW his customers from there  he's taking pictures of me at the beach  he's taking pictures of me for Christmas  cards he's done a lot of other stuff and  he's always gone over and over and over  beyond what I expected from him so Brian  thank you so much from the bottom of my  heart thank you so much for all the  great awesome work and for you watching  guys I'd like you to go and thank  somebody today's thanks somebody who has  had an impact on your business impact on  your life somehow it'll make them feel  great it'll make you feel great it'll  spread good karma out there in the world  and if you guys want to check out  Bryon's website you can check it out at  RC pic studios keep believing thank you  guys for watching I'll see you soon  if you want to see more great content to  keep you inspired motivated and  believing check out my newsletter in the  link below
 

